  Reading: TS{i,cond}, dmt_intensity(i,:), pcb_intensity(i,:), RegDMT2(i,:), RegPCB2(i,:) are all
  indexed by the same loop variable i in 1:nsub, i.e. the authors treat the timeseries subject axis,
  the ratings rows and the LZ rows as one ordering. FD is indexed as columns = subjects
  (FDDMT(TRs, subjects)); its transpose gives one row per subject, but the MATLAB uses FD only at the
  group level (mean over subjects of window FD, and a group-mean partial correlation), so FD-to-subject
  alignment is asserted by the layout, not exercised per subject, in the original code.

