## E. Matched versus mismatched subject pairings (28-bin series, group-mean shape removed)
  Statistic: mean over the 14 matched pairs of Spearman rho between series A_i and B_i, against the
  distribution of the same mean under 20000 random permutations of the B subject labels.
  p is two-sided about the mismatched mean. Alignment predicts matched != mismatched; a null result
  means the two series carry too little subject-specific shape to discriminate, not misalignment.
  A                      B                       matched mismatch       p argmax==self
  ratings_DMT            LZ_DMT                   +0.080   +0.006  0.5636  2/14
  ratings_DMT            FD_DMT                   +0.186   +0.014  0.0763  3/14
  ratings_DMT            sts_gsrglobal_DMT        -0.065   -0.003  0.3360  1/14
  ratings_DMT            TDMI_gsrglobal_DMT       -0.088   -0.009  0.2384  2/14
  LZ_DMT                 FD_DMT                   +0.086   +0.006  0.4008  2/14
